## Calorie Deficit API
This is a simple REST API built with Go that allows users to track their calorie intake and expenditure. The API provides endpoints for managing user profiles, logging food intake, and tracking exercise.

### Folder Structure
```plaintext
calorie_deficit/
├── .air.toml                     # Air configuration for live reloading
├── .env                          # Environment variables
├── .env.example                  # Example environment variables
├── .gitignore                    # Git ignore file
├── go.mod                        # Go module file
├── go.sum                        # Go dependencies checksum
├── main.go                       # Application entry point
├── README                        # Project documentation
├── docker/                       # Docker-related files
│   ├── .env                      # Docker-specific environment variables
│   ├── docker-compose.yml        # Docker Compose configuration
│   └── docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/
│       └── init-user-db.sh       # PostgreSQL initialization script
├── internal/                     # Internal application logic
│   ├── config/
│   │   └── config.go             # Configuration logic
│   ├── constants/
│   │   ├── logMessages.go        # Log message constants
│   │   └── mcp.go                # Constants for MCP (if applicable)
│   ├── handler/
│   │   └── health.go             # Health check handler
│   ├── infrastructure/
│   │   ├── database/
│   │   │   └── postgres/
│   │   │       └── connection.go # Database connection logic
│   │   └── mcp/
│   │       ├── client.go         # MCP client logic
│   │       └── clients/
│   │           ├── openai.go     # OpenAI client implementation
│   │           └── openrouter.go # OpenRouter client implementation
│   └── routes/
│       └── routes.go             # API route definitions
├── pkg/                          # Shared utilities
│   └── logger/
│       └── logger.go             # Logger initialization
├── types/                        # Shared types
│   └── response.go               # Response types
├── utils/                        # Utility functions
│   └── env.go                    # Environment variable utilities
└── tmp/                          # Temporary files
    ├── build-errors.log          # Build error logs
    └── main                      # Temporary build artifacts
```

## Initial Setup
### Environment Variables
- Create a `.env` file in the root directory according to the `.env.example` file.
### POSTGRESQL using Docker Compose
- ``docker-compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up``: This command will start a PostgreSQL database in a Docker container.
### OPEN_ROUTER_AI API KEY
- Obtain an API key from OpenRouterAI and set it in the `.env` file as `OPEN_ROUTER_AI_API_KEY`.

### Next Steps for Development
- Implement the API endpoints 
#### Daily Intake
- Implement Daily Intake logging and retrieval.
- Implement List, Update Meal and Delete Meal.
